Part 5 — Interrupt Boot & Reset Root Password
This is almost guaranteed on the RHCSA exam. There are two methods:
youtube
+1

Method 1: rd.break (Classic)
Reboot the VM → press e at the GRUB menu.

Find the linux line and append rd.break at the end.

Remove rhgb quiet if present (so you see what's happening).

Press Ctrl+X to boot.

You land in an initramfs emergency shell — the real root is mounted read-only at /sysroot.

# Remount /sysroot as read-write
mount -o remount,rw /sysroot

# Chroot into the real system
chroot /sysroot

# Change the root password
passwd root
# (Enter new password twice)

# Tell SELinux to relabel everything on next boot
touch /.autorelabel

# Exit chroot and reboot
exit
exit
# (system reboots and relabels — this can take a few minutes)

Method 2: init=/bin/bash
At GRUB, press e → find the linux line.

Replace everything after root=... with init=/bin/bash (or append it at the end).

Press Ctrl+X.

# Remount root as read-write
mount -o remount,rw /

# Reset password
passwd root

# SELinux relabel
touch /.autorelabel

# Reboot safely
sync
exec /sbin/reboot -f

